# Real financial data — never commit.
# The plan file is the source of truth and lives outside this repo.
plan.json
*.plan.json
plans/
exports/
*.private.json

# Imported transaction data — the most sensitive data in the project.
# The ledger is a separate file from the plan and never enters the repo.
ledger.json
*.ledger.json
imports/
*.csv
*.ofx
*.qif
*.qfx
*.xls
*.xlsx

# Committed fixtures — the demo couple and the golden files (P2-8, P13-4) are
# deliberately tracked, so they are negated back in after the rules above.
# ⚠️ A negation cannot resurrect a file inside an excluded directory. If a
# parent of `fixtures/` is ever added to this file, every line below silently
# stops working and git will not warn you. Never exclude a parent of fixtures/.
!fixtures/
!fixtures/**

# Build output
dist/

# Annual-refresh staging (P2-10). `npm run update-assumptions -- --fy YYYY-YY` writes blanked
# worksheets here for a human to source from. It is scaffolding, not project state: the reviewed
# commit that lands the figures edits src/data/assumptions/ by hand (P2-10b). Nothing imports it
# and tsc does not compile it, so a run can neither change the build nor dirty the tree.
refresh/

# Local scratch
.DS_Store
node_modules/

# Throwaway type-check sandboxes. A mutation pass that wants to know whether a change COMPILES
# writes a one-file case into `.tsc-<kind>-<random>/` and runs `tsc` against it, rather than
# touching the real tree — which is the right instinct, since "does not compile" is a measurement
# and a half-reverted source file makes every later count meaningless. They are per-invocation and
# nothing reads them afterwards, so they are debris rather than state. Ignored here because four of
# them accumulated in one afternoon and an untracked directory nobody recognises is how a real
# stray file comes to be scrolled past.
.tsc-*/

# Agent memory and local agent config — local scratch, not project state.
.claude/

# The Moneysmart HTML snapshot — a dead Angular SPA with no extractable data.
# `docs/moneysmart-limb3-2026-09-18.md` records why it is not worth 13 MB of tree.
docs/Retirement planner - Moneysmart.gov.au.html
docs/Retirement planner - Moneysmart.gov.au_files/
